      "content": "I would advise against trying to manipulate or misrepresent the data to change the facts. This could lead to a more thorough investigation and ultimately damage your company's credibility. Instead, consider framing the payout as a standard, non-admission-of-fault claim under your policy, which is a common practice to limit your exposure while not admitting liability. This approach would avoid making specific claims about the speed or culpability of the driver.",
